==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|es|peh₂w}}
From {{inh|es|la|paucus}}, from {{inh|es|itc-pro|*paukus}}, ultimately from the {{der|es|ine-pro|*peh₂w-||few”, “little}}. Compare {{cog|fr|peu}}, {{cog|it|poco}}, {{cog|pt|pouco}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Adjective===
{{es-adj|f=poca}} (''superlative'' '''[[poquísimo]]''')

# [[little]], not much
#: {{ux|es|Bebí '''poca''' agua.|t=I drank '''little''' water.}}
# [[few]]
#: {{ux|es|Muy '''pocas''' personas hacen eso.|t=Very '''few''' people do that.}}
# [[short]] (time); not [[long]] (ago)
#: {{ux|es|Nos casamos hace '''poco''' tiempo.|t=We got married '''not long''' ago.}}

===Adverb===
{{es-adv}}

# [[little]], not much
#: {{ux|es|Comí '''poco'''.|t=I ate '''little''' / I did'''n’t''' eat '''much'''.}}

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[little]]
#: {{ux|es|Hablo un '''poco''' (de) inglés.|t=I speak a '''little''' English.}}

